MiniFuse control module configuration

Standard audio works through ALSA. Extra switches and hardware meters require
this module, matching kernel headers and selection of one MiniFuse by serial.

After installing the package and matching headers, connect the MiniFuse and run:
  sudo minifuze2-ctl-setup --user YOUR_DESKTOP_ACCOUNT

The setup command detects one connected MiniFuse 2, saves serial selection,
configures control access and loads the module if not already loaded. It does
not reload a running module or change +48V, INST, audio routing or PipeWire.
If several cards are connected, provide --serial explicitly. Existing differing
configuration is retained for manual review. User group access applies after a
fresh login; active local sessions may receive udev access immediately.

An existing manual DKMS installation must be migrated before installing this
package. See https://github.com/Potato83/MiniFuze-for-Linux/blob/main/docs/packages.md
Never force package-file overwrites or remove a working module before ensuring
a matching build is available for the running kernel.
